# Pokemon Yellow Legacy (patched) GameShark .cht for Game Station dual-screen
# Built from cRz-Shadows/Pokemon_Yellow_Legacy pokeyellow.sym (WRAM labels).
# ROM basename Dirt confirmed: PokemonYellowLegacy
#   PokemonYellowLegacy.gbc  ->  PokemonYellowLegacy.cht
# Path on SD: /gbc_cheats/PokemonYellowLegacy.cht
# WARNING: wrong-hack / wrong-version codes can corrupt saves. Backup .sav first.
# Codes load DISABLED; press c in-game, enable only what you need.
# Each "+" part shows as its own menu row (desc #1, #2, ...): turn ON every
# row of the cheat you want, and turn them all OFF again afterwards.
# NEVER use "Enable all" (bag / mart / wild-force codes fight over the same bytes).
#
# === vs Polished Crystal 3.2.3 ===
# Yellow Legacy is Gen1 (pokeyellow-based). Addresses are NOT PC addresses.
# BAG: single Items pocket (wNumBagItems D31C, slot1 D31D/D31E). No Med/Ball
#   pockets. Capacity 59 (hack-expanded; pret vanilla was 20). Money/coins sit
#   AFTER the expanded bag (wPlayerMoney D394, wPlayerCoins D5F1 = pret+0x4E).
# SHINY: SKIPPED — Yellow Legacy has no shiny personality/palette system
#   (no wOTPartyMon1Shiny / Gen2 shiny bit). Cannot mirror PC D29F write.
# RUNNING SHOES: already in the hack as hold-B sprint (home/overworld.asm
#   DoBikeSpeedup when B_BUTTON held). NOT a permanent always-on setting.
#   GS type 01/91 is a full-byte write (no OR): forcing B on hJoyHeld (FFB4)
#   would clobber D-pad/A and break menus/battles. No dedicated always-run
#   WRAM flag exists. Always-run cheat NOT added (unsafe / unmappable).
# ALL TMs/HMs: SKIPPED — Gen1 has no wTMsHMs ownership flag array; TMs are
#   ordinary bag items ($C4+). Stuffing 55 bag slots is not the PC-safe path.
# Big Nugget / Marill / Lugia / Ho-Oh / Pichu / Espeon / Umbreon: Gen2-only or
#   absent from Yellow Legacy — skipped.
# Party happiness: Gen1 party_struct has no happiness byte (skip). Yellow has
#   wPikachuHappiness for the follower only — not mirrored as Party1 happiness.
#
# BAG / ITEM CODES
#  Overwrites bag slot 1 (id@D31D qty@D31E). Bag must already hold >=1 item.
#  Enable 1-2 s, open bag to check, then OFF. Only ONE bag slot cheat at a time.
#  GS writes go into live WRAM; an in-game SAVE makes them permanent.
#
#  RECOVERY: if slot1 is a stuck/wrong item, enable a FIX row briefly, then toss.
#
# MART codes: patch Buy-menu row 1 only (wItemList+1 @ CF7B). Real price comes
#  from ItemPrices in ROM (Master Ball = 0 = free; Rare Candy = 4800).
#  Enable ONLY inside a shop Buy menu; OFF before leaving. ONE mart code at a time.
#
# WILD-FORCE: overwrites all 10 grass + 10 water encounter SPECIES bytes
#  (wGrassMons/wWaterMons level,species pairs @ D887/D8A4). Levels stay map-
#  native. Enable ONE while hunting grass/water; disable after catch.
#  (Per-frame write to wEnemyMonSpecies2 alone is too late: LoadEnemyMonData
#   runs in the same frame as TryDoWildEncounter with no DelayFrame yield.)
#
# PARTY: codes affect party slot 1 — swap the mon you want to the front.
#  Max StatExp = Gen1 EV analogue (HP/Atk/Def/Spe/Spc Exp words @ D17B–D184).
#  Level 100 writes the level byte only; deposit/withdraw or rare-candy to
#  recalc stats if needed. Battle HP writes wBattleMon HP/MaxHP during battle.
#


